                        "glosses": [
                            "北美洲的一些蒿屬（Artemisia）植物的俗稱"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19cb6380-ea40-4513-acfc-bf6dcc6191d6",
                                "sense_id": "f9424580-edd1-31e7-a829-d2455af8acc3",
                                "text": "On our bumpy, mud-soaked ride to the Grand Canyon’s lesser-visited East Rim, a coyote emerged from the sagebrush to lead the way. It took off directly in front of our van, seemingly directing us through a labyrinth of dirt roads. Our guide, a member of the Navajo Nation, parked the vehicle and offered thanks to the coyote for its guidance.",
                                "translation": "我们正前往大峡谷，走的是鲜为人知的东缘道路，路上颠簸泥泞。途中一只郊狼从蒿草丛中窜出，为我们引路。它径直走到我们的面包车前，仿佛在指引我们穿过迷宫般的土路。我们的向导，一位纳瓦霍族人，停好车后向郊狼表示感谢。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
